  "summary": "This study compares six electrochemically evaluated Ti3C2Tx film electrodes: pristine Ti3C2Tx, three holey H-Ti3C2Tx films made using 10, 25, or 40 min O2 oxidation followed by HF removal of TiO2, and two sonication-size controls. All MXene was initially prepared by LiF/HCl etching of Ti3AlC2, and electrochemical tests used 3 M H2SO4 in a three-electrode setup. H-Ti3C2Tx-40 gave the largest explicitly printed gravimetric capacitance, 339 F g\u22121 at 0.5 A g\u22121 for a 25 \u00b5m film; however, H-Ti3C2Tx-25 is the headline thickness-independent electrode, reaching 323 F g\u22121 at 84 \u00b5m and 6.41 mg cm\u22122. The paper does not report BET surface area, porosity, tortuosity, or numerical capacitance values for the individual H-Ti3C2Tx-10 and sonicated controls; oxidized O-Ti3C2Tx intermediates were structurally characterized but not electrochemically reported as electrodes."
}